!pragma layout smetana
' Status: Draft - Reconciliation Incomplete. AI-reconciled; not human reviewed (Principle VII).
' Written source: data-model.md (Membership), BR-22 to BR-24, DEC-08 to DEC-11
title Membership Lifecycle (one row)\nFR-005 to FR-007 (conditional draft: OC-1 open)

[*] --> Active : createGroup / creator, also becomes admin\nor addMember / admin, by exact username

Active : leftAt is empty
Active : full group visibility
Active : may be payer, participant, approver

Ended : leftAt is set; row kept forever
Ended : endedBy = userId means left
Ended : endedBy = admin means removed
Ended : read-only personal history (DEC-07)
Ended : pair balances stay 0.00 (INV-EXIT-1)

state exitChoice <<choice>>

Active --> exitChoice : leaveGroup / member\nor removeMember / admin, on another member
exitChoice --> Active : [a non-zero pair balance in the group,\nor involved in a Pending expense]\nrefused; BusinessRuleException names why
exitChoice --> Ended : [every pair balance is 0.00, and\nnot creator, payer, or participant of a Pending expense]

note right of Ended
  **Rejoin (BR-24):** addMember by an admin creates a **new** row
  starting in Active. This row stays Ended, as history.
  A group with no active members has no admin who can act,
  so no one can rejoin it.
end note

note left of Active
  **Admin departure (BR-23):** when the admin row ends and members remain,
  the earliest-joined remaining active member becomes admin
  (ties by user ID), in the same transaction.
  The last member may leave; the group stays stored with no active members.
  removeMember on oneself is refused: use leaveGroup.
end note

@enduml
